  "lineage": "Telugu kirtana devotional-song genre within the broader Carnatic classical tradition of South India, with Telugu serving as the dominant lyrical language of the Carnatic kriti repertoire. The Telugu-language compositions of the Carnatic Trinity Tyagaraja (1767-1847), Muthuswami Dikshitar (1775-1835), and Syama Sastri (1762-1827) form the canonical core of the entire Carnatic concert repertoire. Performance follows the standard Carnatic kriti structure (pallavi-anupallavi-charanam) with raga-and-tala framework. The Tyagaraja Aradhana annual festival at Tiruvaiyaru constitutes the central institutional anchor of the kriti performance tradition.",
